		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: Backup original flash &amp; eeprom via CPS OpenGD77 support menu]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=1756&amp;p=15231#p15231"><![CDATA[
No it is not possible to backup the flash with the original firmware loaded. As you have found the original firmware does not appear as a com port. This is normal, openGD77 uses different drivers. However loading OpenGD77 does not change any of the calibration or flash settings so a backup immediately after upgrading the firmware is worth doing. <br><br>It is possible to go back to the stock firmware using the standard stock firmware sgl file and loader. <br><br>Colin.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=87">G4EML</a> — Thu Jul 15, 2021 10:43 am</p><hr />
